# Dev server troubleshooting (Windows) — don't chase this as a code bug

Full detail lives in `AGENTS.md → "Local dev server troubleshooting (Windows)"`.
Read that section before spending time editing `vite.config.ts` or blaming a
recent change (e.g. the Lovable `mcpPlugin()`, edge-function CORS work,
zombie `node.exe` processes, or endpoint-security loopback interception —
all investigated and ruled out) when `npm run dev` hangs forever at
`[optimizer] scanning dependencies...` (and a real browser or
browser-automation tool times out waiting for `domcontentloaded` against
`localhost`, even though `curl` returns 200 instantly).

**Confirmed cause:** nested git worktrees checked out inside this repo
(`.claude/worktrees/`, `.worktrees/`, `worktrees/`) each carry a full
`index.html` + `node_modules`. Without a pinned entry, Vite's dependency
scanner globs `**/*.html` from the project root and crawls every one of
them too.

**Fix already applied** in `vite.config.ts`: `optimizeDeps.entries:
["index.html"]` plus `server.watch.ignored` excluding those worktree
directories. If the hang comes back, check `git worktree list` for
accumulated worktrees.
